Assuming you are running on a Raspberry Pi 2-5 or Zero (tested with bookworm Pi5):

1. Install all necessary packages to synthesize top.v and build bit image (top.bin) for the ice4pi:

 sudo apt-get install yosys fpga-icestorm arachne-pnr flashrom
 sudo apt-get install spi-tools
 make

2. Make sure your Pi has SPI enabled (e.g. use raspi-config)

3. Load the top.bin file to the shield:

 sudo make load

---

4. Use SPI to read all 16 GPIB signals at 5MHz sampling rate and send to any TCP/IP connecting client on port 1234:

#!/usr/bin/bash
while [ 1 ] ; do
    dd if=/dev/zero bs=$((64*1024)) iflag=fullblock | /home/pi/spi-tools-0.8.4/src/spi-pipe -d /dev/spidev0.1 --blocksize=$((64*1024)) -s 80000000 | nc -l 0.0.0.0 1234
done

5. You can generate a 1MHz 16 bit clock driving the 16 GPIB signals if you replace top.v with top-counter.v

